  140: ## Bottom line
  141: 
  142: The machinery is sound ג€” the four guards fire correctly with zero observed over-kill, the
  143: final model prices long distinctive piyyut matches at the top, and the deck already
  144: surfaces genuine discovery-grade identifications (2-witness Halevi and Ibn Tzaddik poems)
  145: ג€” but the tier-B deck as sampled is **not yet worth scholar review time below the top
  146: band, and even the Pג‰¥0.8 stratum is ~45% verse/liturgy-chain noise**. One leak family
  147: accounts for nearly all of it: verse/liturgy CHAINS (multi-book chains, ׳•׳’'-abbreviated
  148: quotes, targum/tafsir renderings, statutory formulas) that the single contiguous-window
  149: Bible-alignment test cannot see, and it reaches P=1.00 (Feierberg). Priority fixes, in
  150: leverage order: (1) chain-aware verse guard (windowed alignment coverage instead of one
  151: partial_ratio window); (2) extend canonical masking to Targum/tafsir streams; (3) a
  152: statutory-prayer formula mask + demote-or-flag works that ARE statutory prayers; (4) a
  153: tier-A verse-leak audit for post-classical works (the strict census currently credits ׳¨׳ "׳§
  154: with 70 witnesses and the ׳˜׳•׳¨ with 429 inside the liturgy subcorpus). With (1)ג€“(3) in
  155: place, the observed correct+plausible core (ג‰ˆ30% overall, ג‰ˆ55% at Pג‰¥0.8, plus real finds
  156: even at P=0.43) suggests the re-filtered deck would clear the bar comfortably.
