  209: ### 3. Why the guard misses ג€” diagnosed, with numbers
  210: 
  211: **Cause 1 (dominant): the ֲ±MARGIN=30 hull padding poisons the density check.** Clusters DO
  212: form on the right guard works (flagships: best_cluster 5ג€“44 anchors; raw gram hits 512ג€“3,771
  213: per slice), but every hull is verified over the anchor extent padded ֲ±30 on BOTH sides
  214: (p0=minp-30, p1=maxp+K+30, same on the ref side). For a canonical quote of contiguous length
  215: run, the two mismatched flanks alone drive density ג‰ˆ 60/(run+65): run 30 ג†’ 0.63, 40 ג†’ 0.57,
  216: 50 ג†’ 0.52, 60 ג†’ 0.48, **only run ג‰¥ ~68 clean letters passes 0.45** ג€” higher still under HTR
  217: noise. Verse-chain pieces and statutory formulas are 15ג€“50 letters each, so every hull fails
  218: verification and coverage is exactly 0.00. This also explains WHICH cases it did catch: the
  219: three old-DEM cards with long contiguous runs (scores 72.7ג€“79.1). `GUARD_COVER_MIN=0.55` is
  220: NOT the issue (missed leaks measure 0.00, not 0.45ג€“0.54); `MIN_SPAN=30` is not binding
  221: (padded spans are ג‰¥65 by construction).
  222: 
  223: **Cause 2: guard-reference gaps.** The 13 Liturgy units are 5ֳ—׳¢׳׳™׳“׳”, 3ֳ—׳‘׳¨׳›׳•׳× ׳©׳׳¢, 2ֳ—׳§׳™׳“׳•׳©,
  224: ׳”׳׳, ׳‘׳¨׳›׳× ׳”׳׳–׳•׳, ׳”׳’׳“׳”. Probed for the formulas behind my statutory leaks: **׳›׳ ׳—׳׳™׳¨׳ ג€”
  225: absent from all 60 guard works** (exists in the full ref only inside M:Ytext507000); kaddish
  226: (׳™׳×׳’׳“׳) absent; ׳”׳׳₪׳™׳ absent; ׳©׳”׳—׳™׳™׳ ׳• present only via the Haggadah unit (spelling ׳©׳”׳—׳™׳ ׳•);
  227: ׳‘׳¨׳›׳•׳× ׳ ׳™׳©׳•׳׳™׳ absent. No threshold can catch what the reference doesn't contain.
  228: 
  229: **Cause 3 ג€” ruled out: DF-cap.** Only 1,830 gram codes are DF-dropped (>128 postings) from
  230: the 3.24M-posting guard index; flagship slices retain 65ג€“90% of their grams with ג‰¥1 posting
